WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
Speaker 1: I'm going to play something very&nbsp;
interesting for you today. It's delusional. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:10.560
deranged, it's backwards as much of the American&nbsp;
right wing is. But it opens up a very interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.440
conversation. A Republican candidate for&nbsp;
governor, Mark Robinson, who happens to be black,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:21.360
and this is very relevant to what we're going&nbsp;
to hear from him. He is in favor of reparations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:30.000
but not the kind you might think of. What&nbsp;
Mark Robinson says he wants for reparations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.000
is black people should give white people&nbsp;
reparations as a thank you for ending slavery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.040
Yes. Now, I know you're saying. Wait, but, David,&nbsp;
that doesn't make sense for so many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.440
reasons, of course. But let's first listen to&nbsp;
what he had to say in its full ridiculous glory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.720
and then we will talk about it.
Speaker 4: So the people that we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.635
talking about, reparations in this country,&nbsp;
they want reparations. And I remember I made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.635 --> 00:00:53.880
this particular liberal so angry at&nbsp;
me because I told them right to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:10.200
face. Nobody owes you anything for slavery. If&nbsp;
you want to tell the truth about it, it is you who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:18.540
owns Edgehill. Whoa, whoa. Why do you? Because&nbsp;
somebody in those fields took strikes for you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:26.520
Somebody after those fields were ended in slavery&nbsp;
was ended. Somebody had to walk through Jim Crow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:36.180
for you. Somebody fought wars and died for you.&nbsp;
Somebody lived left dead because they didn't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:43.140
what you have, and they did it for you. Hmm.&nbsp;
There are people in their graves right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.520
and they are there because they were&nbsp;
willing to stand up and fight for you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:55.680
Those folks on the Edmund Pettus Bridge. Carry&nbsp;
an American flags. Take that Colin Kaepernick.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:02.040
Living in a society that he could scarcely&nbsp;
acknowledge. Something he has never know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:08.040
Living with a bigotry that none of us can&nbsp;
imagine. Right. Carried American flags on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:12.960
that bridge. And when they were hit upside&nbsp;
the head with nightsticks and shot with water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:18.720
hoses and knocked to the ground, they got&nbsp;
up and put those flags up and kept marching.&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.680
Speaker 1: All right. So I guess he's&nbsp;
saying not only do black people today&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:31.320
owe white people reparations, they also know&nbsp;
earlier black folks who are no longer alive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:37.800
reparations, which is weird. So this is this&nbsp;
is unreal stuff. And this is what happens when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.240
you just become a contrarian for the sake of&nbsp;
contrarianism. Now, I think that there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.360
perfectly reasonable critiques about reparations,&nbsp;
and we've talked about them before. You can come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:54.540
down on either side as far as reparations go. But&nbsp;
the idea that black people owe white people money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:02.220
for freeing them from slavery, ignoring that&nbsp;
they were the ones enslaving the black folks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:08.400
to begin with is really something else. It's like&nbsp;
asking for praise, for putting out a fire that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:14.700
started. And the other important thing to remember&nbsp;
is that many white people, including the slave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.800
owners, didn't want to end slavery. He's sort&nbsp;
of pretending like, listen, white people ended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.840
slavery, so you should thank them. No, no, no, no.&nbsp;
A whole bunch of white people did not want to end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:32.820
slavery, and they lost the Civil War over that.&nbsp;
It's a wacky argument to make. And by the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:40.500
even after slavery was legally abolished, we still&nbsp;
saw black folks facing segregation of all kinds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:47.760
discrimination, oppression in the form of Jim Crow&nbsp;
laws, systemic racism. And so much of that legacy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:53.280
that we followed through hundreds of years. This&nbsp;
is really wild, and I'll be totally honest with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.280 --> 00:04:00.840
you. I don't even know if Robinson genuinely&nbsp;
believes this. This is the virus, the mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:08.580
virus of Contrarianism of. If anybody on the left&nbsp;
is suggesting X, then I need to make clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:13.500
the opposite of X is actually what we need.&nbsp;
I don't know whether this is going to win him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:20.220
the governorship or what, but it is unreal to see&nbsp;
them saying these things out loud. And what's even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:26.100
crazier is people in the crowd who decide to clap&nbsp;
for it. This country has fallen very, very far.

